@ 2:12  expr ::= te|rm { "+" term }* ;
  2:10-2:14 "term"
  | **rule** `term`
  |
  | ```
  | term = "1" | "2" ;
  | ```
  |
  | Defined 2 times (lines 3, 4): v12 draws each rule, and the name refers to the first.
@ 2:27  expr ::= term { "+" term }|* ;
  2:27-2:28 "*"
  | **`*`**
  |
  | `e*`: `e` any number of times, or not at all. Postfixes stack: `e?*`.
@ 3:12  term = "1" || "2" ;
  3:12-3:13 "|"
  | **`|`**
  |
  | `a | b`: one of the alternatives.
@ 4:3  te|rm = "again" ;
  4:1-4:5 "term"
  | **rule** `term`
  |
  | ```
  | term = "1" | "2" ;
  | ```
  |
  | Defined 2 times (lines 3, 4): v12 draws each rule, and the name refers to the first.
